From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: stop gen1 rate control reading buffer timestamps

SM8250 overshoots its target by a wide margin: Steam asks for 12 Mbit/s
and gameplay comes out at 20-73 Mbit/s, tracking the content. gen2 holds
the target.

By default the gen1 firmware works out the time between frames from the
buffer timestamps, which it expects in microseconds. iris passes the
vb2 timestamp through in nanoseconds, so frames look 1000 times further
apart than they are and rate control has a far larger budget per frame
than the target allows. The same value comes back on the capture buffer,
so userspace sees correct timestamps.

gen2 avoids this by turning off time-delta-based rate control. Do the
same on gen1 with HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP, which
makes the firmware derive the delta from the input frame rate. The
property has the opposite sense to the gen2 one, hence value 1. The
vendor driver sends it on every session.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
index abe8e032d..073378eae 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
@@ -1558,7 +1558,7 @@ int iris_set_time_delta_based_rc(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_c
 	u32 value = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].value;
 
 	/*
-	 * Disable time-delta-based rate control (value = 0).
+	 * Disable time-delta-based rate control (value = 0 on gen2, 1 on gen1).
 	 * This overrides the firmware's default (enabled), ensuring the
 	 * firmware uses the configured bitrate target rather than calculating
 	 * bitrate from frame timing.
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
index 4f2ab19b4..b11a31edc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
@@ -149,6 +149,17 @@ static const struct platform_inst_fw_cap inst_fw_cap_sm8250_enc[] = {
 		.flags = CAP_FLAG_OUTPUT_PORT | CAP_FLAG_MENU,
 		.set = iris_set_bitrate_mode_gen1,
 	},
+	{
+		/* The gen1 property disables, so 1 here is 0 on gen2. */
+		.cap_id = TIME_DELTA_BASED_RC,
+		.min = 0,
+		.max = 1,
+		.step_or_mask = 1,
+		.value = 1,
+		.hfi_id = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP,
+		.flags = CAP_FLAG_OUTPUT_PORT,
+		.set = iris_set_time_delta_based_rc,
+	},
 	{
 		.cap_id = FRAME_SKIP_MODE,
 		.min = V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_SKIP_MODE_DISABLED,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 867e00724..2e249c5d8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -602,7 +602,8 @@ iris_hfi_gen1_packet_session_set_property(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *p
 		packet->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(*pl);
 		break;
 	}
-	case HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_SYNC_FRAME_SEQUENCE_HEADER: {
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_SYNC_FRAME_SEQUENCE_HEADER:
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP: {
 		struct hfi_enable *en = prop_data;
 		u32 *in = pdata;
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
index 275f3fea3..fb3b3f1f2 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_defines.h
@@ -155,6 +155,7 @@
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_LTRMODE				0x200501c
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_MAX_NUM_B_FRAMES		0x2005020
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_HIER_P_MAX_NUM_ENH_LAYER	0x2005026
+#define HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP		0x2005027
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_TARGET_BITRATE			0x2006001
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_INTRA_PERIOD			0x2006003
 #define HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME		0x2006004
